From a57c887612c8463de8108337618c2555fa851fdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepFox Maintainers <maintainers@sheepfox.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:33:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Optimise WebRender and canvas defaults for speed

Bake the three highest-impact rendering defaults into the binary:

  * gfx.webrender.precache-shaders=true  pre-compiles shader programs at startup
    instead of on the first scroll/animation, removing first-frame hitching.
  * gfx.content.skia-font-cache-size=20   (from 5 MB) keeps glyph rasters hot for
    text-heavy pages.
  * gfx.canvas.accelerated.cache-size=128 (from 256 MB) halves the worst-case
    Canvas surface cache - this is a low-RAM profile, and 512 MB of resident
    canvas surfaces was the single biggest regression against that goal.

Deliberately NOT changed here: gfx.webrender.all and layers.gpu-process.enabled.
Firefox decides those per GPU/driver at runtime, and forcing them on unsupported
hardware is the classic source of GPU-process crashes. SheepFox sets
gfx.webrender.all in config/modules/01-speedfox.js where a user can revert it,
and never disables layers.gpu-process.enabled, so GPU crashes stay isolated.
---
 modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
index 80be46d..ae03320 100644
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -7425,7 +7425,7 @@
 
 - name: gfx.canvas.accelerated.cache-size
   type: RelaxedAtomicUint32
-  value: 256
+  value: 128
   mirror: always
 
 - name: gfx.canvas.accelerated.reserve-empty-cache
@@ -7780,7 +7780,7 @@
 # Size in megabytes
 - name: gfx.content.skia-font-cache-size
   type: int32_t
-  value: 5
+  value: 20
   mirror: once
 
 - name: gfx.device-reset.limit
@@ -8730,7 +8730,7 @@
 
 - name: gfx.webrender.precache-shaders
   type: bool
-  value: false
+  value: true
   mirror: once
 
 # When gl debug message is a high severity message, forwward it to gfx critical
